        <item>
            <title>0.27.1</title>
            <pubDate>Mon, 26 Oct 2026 16:30:15 -0500</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>61</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.27.1</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <description><![CDATA[<style>:root{color-scheme:light dark}body{font:13px/1.45 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,system-ui,sans-serif;color:#1d1d1f;margin:0;padding:2px 4px}h3{font-size:13px;font-weight:600;margin:0 0 6px}ul{margin:0;padding-left:18px}li{margin:0 0 4px}code{font:12px ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace}@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){body{color:#f5f5f7}}</style><h3>What's new in Keeploop 0.27.1</h3><ul><li>Keeploop no longer turns on Open at login by itself. Turn it on in Settings &gt; General if you want Keeploop to start when you log in.</li><li>If remote access cannot start, Settings now says why. Turning remote access off clears the message.</li><li>Signing in again on a Mac you already paired replaces its old entry instead of adding a second Mac. If Sign out does not finish, Keeploop now tells you why.</li><li>Web and phone AI apps are now told when your Keeploop tools change, for example after you turn on a source, so they can pick up the new tools.</li><li>The page where you approve an AI app now shows whether each Mac is online, or when it was last seen.</li></ul>]]></description>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>26.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
